1. AZURE ENDPOINTS
What Is Endpoint?

Endpoint means:
Destination/service address where communication happens.

Simple meaning:
where traffic goes
Example
When VM sends logs to Azure Monitor:
VM
↓
https://monitor.azure.com
That URL/service is an endpoint.

Types of Azure Endpoints
| Type             | Example                     |
| ---------------- | --------------------------- |
| Public endpoint  | internet reachable          |
| Private endpoint | private VNet IP             |
| Service endpoint | secure Azure service access |

2. AZURE MONITOR INGESTION ENDPOINT

What Is Ingestion Endpoint?

Ingestion endpoint means:
Azure Monitor service endpoint that RECEIVES telemetry/logs/metrics.

VM
↓
AMA Agent
↓
Azure Monitor Ingestion Endpoint
↓
Log Analytics Workspace

Default Communication
Usually:
HTTPS 443 over public Azure endpoint

IMPORTANT
Ingestion endpoint is Azure-managed service.
You normally do NOT manually create it

3. PRIVATE ENDPOINT
By default:
Telemetry may travel through:

public internet/Azure public endpoints
Even though encrypted.
Banks/fintech often dislike this.

Solution
Private Endpoint.

What Is Private Endpoint?

Private endpoint gives Azure service:

private IP inside your VNet
Instead of public access.

Example

Without private endpoint:
VM
↓
Public Azure Monitor endpoint
With private endpoint:
VM
↓
Private IP in VNet
↓
Azure Service

Example Services Supporting Private Endpoint
| Service         | Example               |
| --------------- | --------------------- |
| Storage Account | private blob access   |
| KeyVault        | private secret access |
| SQL Database    | private DB access     |
| Azure Monitor   | private telemetry     |


