VERY IMPORTANT NETWORKING UNDERSTANDING
Private Endpoint creates:
NIC + Private IP inside subnet

This is why DNS becomes important

DNS FLOW

Without proper DNS:

VM may still resolve:public Azure endpoint
instead of private endpoint.
So enterprises configure:
private DNS zones
conditional forwarding


-------------------------------------------------------------------------

FIRST UNDERSTAND THE PROBLEM

Normally Azure services use:

public DNS names

Example:
myworkspace.ods.opinsights.azure.com

This resolves to:
public IP

So VM traffic goes to public Azure endpoint.

Even though encrypted.

ENTERPRISE REQUIREMENT
Company says:
No monitoring traffic over public internet.

So we use:
Private Endpoint
Private DNS

WHAT ACTUALLY HAPPENS WHEN PRIVATE ENDPOINT CREATED?
VERY IMPORTANT.
When you create Private Endpoint for Azure Monitor:

Azure creates:
Network Interface Card (NIC)

inside YOUR subnet.

Example

VNet:

10.1.0.0/16

Subnet:

10.1.2.0/24
Azure Creates NIC

Example:

monitor-pe-nic

with private IP:

10.1.2.5
VERY IMPORTANT

That private IP represents:

Azure Monitor service

inside your VNet.

NORMAL FLOW (Without Private Endpoint)
VM
↓
DNS resolves public IP
↓
Public Azure Monitor endpoint
↓
Azure Monitor
PRIVATE FLOW
VM
↓
DNS resolves private IP
↓
10.1.2.5 (Private Endpoint NIC)
↓
Azure Backbone Network
↓
Azure Monitor

This is the key architecture.

WHY DNS IMPORTANT?

Because application/AMA still accesses:

myworkspace.ods.opinsights.azure.com

NOT:

10.1.2.5

DNS must translate:

public hostname → private IP
THIS IS THE MOST IMPORTANT CONCEPT

Private Endpoint works properly ONLY if DNS resolves to private IP.

Otherwise:
traffic still goes public.

HOW PRIVATE DNS ZONE HELPS

Azure Private DNS Zone stores:

private DNS records
Example

Public:

myworkspace.ods.opinsights.azure.com
→ 20.x.x.x

Private DNS:

myworkspace.privatelink.ods.opinsights.azure.com
→ 10.1.2.5
WHAT HAPPENS INTERNALLY?

VM asks:

What is myworkspace.ods.opinsights.azure.com?

Private DNS responds:

10.1.2.5

instead of public IP.

COMPLETE FLOW
VM
↓
DNS Query
↓
Private DNS Zone
↓
Returns Private IP
↓
Traffic goes to Private Endpoint NIC
↓
Azure Backbone
↓
Azure Monitor

HOW TO CONFIGURE PRIVATE DNS ZONE
Step 1 — Create Private Endpoint

Portal:

Azure Monitor
→ Private Link Scope
→ Private Endpoint

Choose:

VNet
subnet
Step 2 — Azure Creates NIC

Example:

10.1.2.5
Step 3 — Create Private DNS Zone

Example:

privatelink.monitor.azure.com

OR:

privatelink.ods.opinsights.azure.com

depends on service.

Step 4 — Link DNS Zone To VNet

Very important.

Private DNS Zone
↓
Virtual Network Link
↓
Your VNet

Now VMs inside VNet can resolve private records.

Step 5 — Verify DNS

Inside VM:

nslookup myworkspace.ods.opinsights.azure.com

Should return:

10.x.x.x

NOT public IP.

HOW CONDITIONAL FORWARDING FITS?

This is hybrid enterprise networking topic.

Used when:

on-prem DNS servers

need to resolve Azure private DNS.

REAL ENTERPRISE SCENARIO

On-prem server wants:

myworkspace.ods.opinsights.azure.com

But on-prem DNS doesn't know Azure private zones.

Solution

Conditional Forwarding.

WHAT IS CONDITIONAL FORWARDING?

DNS rule:

If domain matches Azure private zone,
forward DNS query to Azure DNS resolver.
Example

On-prem DNS config:

*.privatelink.monitor.azure.com
→ forward to Azure DNS
FLOW WITH CONDITIONAL FORWARDING
On-prem Server
↓
On-prem DNS
↓
Conditional Forwarder
↓
Azure DNS Private Resolver
↓
Private DNS Zone
↓
Private IP Returned
MODERN ENTERPRISE AZURE DESIGN

Usually:

Hub VNet
 ├── Azure Firewall
 ├── DNS Resolver
 ├── Private DNS Zones
 └── Monitoring

Spoke VNets
 ├── AKS
 ├── VMs
 └── Apps

All workloads use centralized DNS/private monitoring.

IMPORTANT DNS COMPONENTS
| Component             | Role                         |
| --------------------- | ---------------------------- |
| Private Endpoint      | private IP                   |
| NIC                   | network interface holding IP |
| Private DNS Zone      | maps hostname → private IP   |
| VNet Link             | allows VNet to use zone      |
| Conditional Forwarder | forwards DNS queries         |
| Azure DNS Resolver    | resolves Azure private DNS   |

COMMON TROUBLESHOOTING SCENARIO
Issue

Private endpoint created,
BUT traffic still public.

Root Cause

DNS still resolving:

public IP

instead of private IP.

Verification
nslookup myworkspace.ods.opinsights.azure.com
Expected
10.x.x.x
Wrong Result
20.x.x.x

means public resolution still happening.

VERY COMMON INTERVIEW QUESTION
Question

Why is Private DNS required for Private Endpoint?

Strong Answer

Private Endpoints provide private IP addresses for Azure services inside VNets, but clients still access services using standard Azure DNS names. Private DNS Zones ensure those hostnames resolve to private IPs instead of public endpoints, allowing traffic to stay within Azure private backbone networks.

Excellent senior-level answer.

